# SHA-256 hashes for compiled Soroban WASM artifacts — issue #410
#
# Generated by: bash scripts/verify-wasm-hashes.sh --generate \
#                 contracts/target/wasm32-unknown-unknown/release
#
# To regenerate after an intentional change:
#   bash scripts/verify-wasm-hashes.sh --generate \
#     contracts/target/wasm32-unknown-unknown/release
#
# CI verifies every PR and push against this file. If the hashes diverge the
# build fails, preventing accidental or malicious WASM substitution.
#
# Format: "<sha256>  <path>" (two spaces, as produced by sha256sum).
# Lines starting with '#' are ignored by the verification script.
#
# ── Hashes will be committed here after the first CI build ──────────────────
#
# Example (replace with real output from --generate):
# a3f...  contracts/target/wasm32-unknown-unknown/release/lending_pool.wasm
# b8c...  contracts/target/wasm32-unknown-unknown/release/loan_manager.wasm
# d1e...  contracts/target/wasm32-unknown-unknown/release/multisig_governance.wasm
# f2a...  contracts/target/wasm32-unknown-unknown/release/remittance_nft.wasm
